      "text": [
        " اَلطَّوَافِ.\nوَ فِي رِوَايَةِ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ اَلْفُضَيْلِ عَنِ اَلرَّبِيعِ بْنِ خُثَيْمٍ : أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَفْعَلُ ذَلِكَ كُلَّمَا بَلَغَ إِلَى اَلرُّكْنِ اَلْيَمَانِيِّ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2820 - It is narrated from Abu Basir:\n\"Imam Abu Abdullah (as) fell ill, so he instructed his attendants to carry him and circumambulate the Kaaba with him. He ordered them to drag his foot on the ground so that his feet would touch the ground during the circumambulation.\"\nAnd in another narration by Muhammad ibn al-Fudhayl from Al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym:\n\"He would do this whenever he reached the Yemeni Corner (al-Rukn al-Yamani).\""
        ]
      }
    },
